From 9d722167852fadb3b8f953a7a73edb633be80c5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:00:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 058/146] hydra: a texture coming from a COP came out flipped

The V inversion reported for several days came neither from the UVs nor from
the MaterialX translation: it only affects textures read through an `op:` path,
that is, the only image path we write ourselves.

`hou.saveImageDataToFile` writes the first row of the data as the top scanline -
its documentation says so - whereas a COP's buffer starts at the bottom, the
Houdini way. We passed it the buffer as is: the image came out flipped, and it
looked like an inverted V that had to be corrected by hand with a factor -1. The
function offers a `flip_vertical` made for this; it is now set.

Measurement of the function's contract, without a COP: an array whose first row
is white comes out with that row at the **top** of the file. The rest of the
chain is out of hython's reach - Copernicus does not compile its OpenCL kernels
there, with or without our package - so the final confirmation is done in the
viewport.

What it was not, verified in passing: five UV paths measured, all upright,
including the exact mesh of the reported scene - a `leftHanded` quad with a
faceVarying `st` - which Karma and we render identically.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hydra/houdini_cop.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hydra/houdini_cop.cpp b/src/hydra/houdini_cop.cpp
index e745f01d..a959651e 100644
--- a/src/hydra/houdini_cop.cpp
+++ b/src/hydra/houdini_cop.cpp
@@ -123,9 +123,15 @@ std::string ResolveHoudiniCopPath(const std::string &path)
                            "                    _dst[1::4] = _src[1::_c]\n"
                            "                    _dst[2::4] = _src[2::_c] if _c > 2 else _src[1::_c]\n"
                            "                _dst[3::4] = array.array('f', [1.0]) * _px\n"
+                           /* `flip_vertical`, et il le faut : hou.saveImageDataToFile
+                            * ecrit la premiere ligne de donnees comme scanline du haut
+                            * - c'est sa documentation - alors que le buffer d'un COP
+                            * commence en bas, a la maniere d'Houdini. Sans ce drapeau
+                            * la texture sort retournee, ce qui se voit comme un V
+                            * inverse et se corrige a la main par un facteur -1. */
                            "            hou.saveImageDataToFile(_dst, _w, _h, '" +
                            outPath +
-                           "')\n"
+                           "', True)\n"
                            "except Exception:\n"
                            "    pass\n";
 
